// FIELD SERVICE — NIGHT DRIVE — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FIELD SERVICE as synthwave — a game alternate of plumber, selectable from the
// dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// The hook stays the hook: the verse plays it at HALF SPEED (a chord a bar, a hollow
// PWM lead), the chorus at its own speed on a gliding hero lead with an ice-bell
// octave over it and a chord every half bar — which is the rate the tune always
// implied (| Am F | C G | for the A phrase, | Am C | F G | for B). A rising
// sequence of the hook's opening figure is the pre-chorus. Chorus two is a whole
// step up, in B minor.
// 
//   1–4    intro — string pad, crystal arp, sub (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–12   verse — the hook at half speed, A then B phrase
//   13–16  pre — the head of the hook climbing F, G, Am, E7; snare roll, riser
//   17–32  chorus — A A B B A A C C, 16th octave bass, four on the floor
//   33–40  breakdown — electric grand and glass choir, C then A phrase half speed
//   41–44  build — the pre a whole step up
//   45–60  chorus two — B minor, brass throughout
//   61–64  turnaround — back to A minor; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// 64 bars at 118. Written by work/local/_fs-remix-night-drive.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): stutter rolls into both choruses (16, 44); the glass choir swells into the breakdown, the grand fades into the build.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
